THIRD PARTY LICENSES
====================

dio-domains is distributed as source (this repository) and as a container image.
The image bundles third-party software. This file lists what is shipped, the
license of each component, and where the full license text can be found.

The image includes this file and the referenced texts under
/usr/share/licenses/dio/, together with a manifest of every installed
OCaml/opam package (name, version, license) at 
/usr/share/licenses/dio/opam-packages.txt, generated from the build switch.


================================================================================
1. OCaml / OxCaml runtime
================================================================================

The dio and dio-dashboard executables are compiled with, and statically link,
the OCaml runtime (libasmrun) from OxCaml, Jane Street's fork of OCaml. The
image is built with the 5.2.0+ox switch (ocaml-variants.5.2.0+ox,
oxcaml-compiler.5.2.0minus40).

License: the OCaml Core System (files marked "Copyright INRIA") is distributed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1, with the standard
OCaml linking exception. That exception permits linking the Core System into an
executable and distributing the result under terms of your choice, without the
additional requirements of LGPL clause 6. Files marked "Copyright Jane Street"
and not "Copyright INRIA" are distributed under the MIT license.

Full text: third_party/OCaml-LICENSE (the upstream OxCaml LICENSE, containing
the linking exception and the complete LGPL-2.1 and MIT texts).

Source: https://github.com/oxcaml/oxcaml


